  "notes": "Chabot College's own courses for the Plan (spec 24 → Data, college_courses). Code, title and units are copied from the course descriptions in Chabot's 2025-2026 catalog PDF on chabotcollege.edu (linked from https://www.chabotcollege.edu/courses/archives.php), the newest catalog Chabot hosts itself. Chabot's current catalog, the 2026-27 online catalog on chabot.curriqunet.com (linked from https://www.chabotcollege.edu/courses/index.php), answers 403 to scripts, so nothing here was compared with it: a person checks each row against it. source_url is the PDF with #page= set to the PDF page (two more than the printed page number) that holds the course description. The 2025-2026 catalog prints no C-ID on any course description, so c_id is null on every row; nothing was looked up elsewhere. Topics come from the course title against the topic, or, for the TMC lists (comm-list-*, econ-list-*, polisci-*, psych-list-*, sociology-list-*, business-math, econ-calculus, math-list-a, statistics slots), the list in Chabot's own AA-T or AS-T page for that major in the same catalog (PDF pages: Biology AS-T 171-172, Business Administration 2.0 AS-T 175, Communication Studies 2.0 AA-T 200-201, Economics AA-T 226-227, Mathematics AS-T 304, Political Science AA-T 351-352, Psychology AA-T 368, Sociology AA-T 377-378). Chabot has no CS AS-T (only an AS). A course in an ADT list also gets the later list topics that say any course not already used (psych List A to B to C, comm List A to B, sociology List A to B, econ List A to B, polisci core to List A to List B, math List A to List B). Chabot's Mathematics AS-T has List A (one of MTH 4 or MTH 6) and List B (programming, physics, discrete math, statistics, or the unused List A course); math-list-a is given to Chabot's List B courses, the closest list, the way LPC gave STAT C1000 math-list-a; diff-eq-and-linear-algebra is given to MTH 4 and MTH 6 by title. biology-first is BIOS 21A, the one course of the BIOS 21A-21C series with no biology or chemistry prerequisite. cs1 is on CSCI 15 and CSCI 19A, which the catalog says are designed for CS I, and on CSCI 14 with a todo. PHIL 55 Symbolic Logic gets comm-logic-computing-culture because the topic names symbolic logic. physics-year is on the courses covering mechanics or electricity and magnetism (PHYS 4A, 4B, 7A, 7C), as LPC did. comm-intro and science-extra have no Chabot course here: the catalog doesn't make a match plain, so students type their own course for those (LPC did the same). Left out: courses with no topic a Chabot page plainly supports, including ANTH 1, CSCI 7, ECN 10, MTH 33S, PHYS 4C, PHYS 5, PHYS 7D, HLTH 8 and the HIS courses. Todos: COMM 48 units (catalog prints 1-4), CSCI 14 cs1, ECN 1 and ECN 2 (Las Positas renumbered ECON 1 and 2 as ECON C2001 and C2002 from Fall 2026; check Chabot's 2026-27 catalog), MTH 43S statistics, PHYS 7B science-second. Every row is the 2025-2026 catalog and may have changed in 2026-27, so a person checks each row against Chabot's 2026-27 catalog. Then run: npm run import -- data/raw/planning/college-courses-chabot.json --dry-run",
